Remove Whitelabel toggle, widen and reorder the Service dropdown (v0.114)

Whitelabel toggle removal: the v0.113 fix for the stale-bearer-token bug
turned out to have been the real blocker on DPD's own account-level
whitelabel template the whole time - now that it's fixed, whitelabelling
works correctly from DPD's side without any in-request workaround. Reverted
DpdShippingService.buildRequestBody() back to always sending the real
sender address, postcode and contact phone in collectionDetails, and
removed the Whitelabel checkbox/postcode field and their settings sync from
Settings.tsx (dpd_whitelabel_collection_address, dpd_whitelabel_postcode -
left as harmless orphaned rows in Settings if already saved, just no longer
read or written).

Service dropdown: the "Service" select on the order despatch panel was
fixed at w-56 (14rem) regardless of how much space was actually free in the
panel, cutting off longer service names. Its wrapping div is now flex-1
with a 20rem minimum, so it grows to fill whatever room the row has instead
of a fixed width. Also reordered the options: Expak 1, then Expak 5, then
Parcel services (BNS's three most-used) are grouped first via a stable sort
on networkDesc, with everything else left in DPD's own returned order.

